# Flutter Component: SizedBox

## 1. What is `SizedBox`?

`SizedBox` is a Flutter widget used mainly to:

* Give a widget a **specific width or height**
* Create **empty space** between widgets
* Constrain a child's size

Think of `SizedBox` as a **simple box with a fixed size**.

```text
┌─────────────────────────┐
│                         │
│      SizedBox           │
│                         │
└─────────────────────────┘
```

---

# 2. Basic Syntax

```dart
SizedBox(
  width: 200,
  height: 100,
)
```

You can also put a child inside it:

```dart
SizedBox(
  width: 200,
  height: 100,
  child: Text("Hello"),
)
```

---

# 3. `width`

Sets the width.

```dart
SizedBox(
  width: 200,
  child: Text("Hello"),
)
```

The child gets a width of approximately 200 logical pixels within the available constraints.

---

# 4. `height`

Sets the height.

```dart
SizedBox(
  height: 100,
  child: Text("Hello"),
)
```

---

# 5. `width` + `height`

You can control both:

```dart
SizedBox(
  width: 200,
  height: 100,
  child: Text("Hello"),
)
```

Conceptually:

```text
<--------- 200 --------->

┌────────────────────────┐
│                        │
│         Hello          │  ↑
│                        │  │ 100
└────────────────────────┘  ↓
```

---

# 6. `SizedBox` for Spacing

This is one of its **most common uses**.

Suppose you have:

```dart
Column(
  children: [
    Text("Username"),
    Text("Password"),
  ],
)
```

There may not be enough space between them.

Use:

```dart
Column(
  children: [
    Text("Username"),

    SizedBox(
      height: 20,
    ),

    Text("Password"),
  ],
)
```

Result:

```text
Username


Password
```

The `SizedBox` creates the empty vertical space.

---

# 7. Horizontal Spacing

Inside a `Row`, use `width`.

```dart
Row(
  children: [
    Icon(Icons.person),

    SizedBox(
      width: 10,
    ),

    Text("Rahul"),
  ],
)
```

Result:

```text
👤     Rahul
       ↑
     10 px
```

So remember:

```text
Column → SizedBox(height: ...)
Row    → SizedBox(width: ...)
```

This is one of the most useful beginner rules.

---

# 8. `SizedBox` Without a Child

You can use it only for spacing.

```dart
SizedBox(
  height: 20,
)
```

There is no child.

It simply creates a 20-pixel vertical gap.

Similarly:

```dart
SizedBox(
  width: 20,
)
```

creates horizontal space.

---

# 9. `SizedBox` With a Child

You can constrain a widget's size.

```dart
SizedBox(
  width: 200,
  height: 100,
  child: Container(
    color: Colors.blue,
  ),
)
```

Here:

```text
SizedBox
   ↓
Container
```

The SizedBox provides the size constraints.

---

# 10. `SizedBox.expand()`

`SizedBox.expand()` tells the child to **take all available space**.

```dart
SizedBox.expand(
  child: Container(
    color: Colors.blue,
  ),
)
```

Conceptually:

```text
┌─────────────────────────────┐
│                             │
│                             │
│        BLUE AREA            │
│                             │
│                             │
└─────────────────────────────┘
```

This can be useful when you want a child to fill the available constraints.

---

# 11. `SizedBox.shrink()`

`SizedBox.shrink()` creates a box that attempts to take the **smallest possible size**.

```dart
SizedBox.shrink()
```

This is useful in conditional UI.

For example:

```dart
isLoading
    ? CircularProgressIndicator()
    : SizedBox.shrink()
```

If `isLoading` is false, the widget occupies minimal space.

---

# 12. `const SizedBox`

When the dimensions are constant, you can use `const`.

```dart
const SizedBox(
  height: 20,
)
```

This is commonly seen in Flutter code.

Example:

```dart
Column(
  children: [
    const Text("Username"),

    const SizedBox(
      height: 20,
    ),

    const Text("Password"),
  ],
)
```

---

# 13. `SizedBox` vs `Container`

This is an important distinction.

### `SizedBox`

Main purpose:

```text
Size + Space
```

Example:

```dart
SizedBox(
  height: 20,
)
```

### `Container`

Main purpose:

```text
Size + Space + Decoration + Alignment + Background
```

Example:

```dart
Container(
  width: 200,
  height: 100,

  padding: EdgeInsets.all(20),

  decoration: BoxDecoration(
    color: Colors.blue,
    borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(20),
  ),
)
```

### Simple rule

If you only need:

> "I need 20 pixels of space."

Use:

```dart
SizedBox(height: 20)
```

Don't create a Container just for that.

---

# 14. `SizedBox` vs `Padding`

These are also different.

### `SizedBox`

Creates fixed space:

```dart
SizedBox(
  height: 20,
)
```

### `Padding`

Adds space **inside/around a child**:

```dart
Padding(
  padding: EdgeInsets.all(20),
  child: Text("Hello"),
)
```

Think:

```text
SizedBox
→ Empty/fixed-size space or size constraint

Padding
→ Space around a specific child
```

---

# 15. Real-World Example — Login Screen

Suppose you have:

```dart
Column(
  children: [
    Text("Login"),

    SizedBox(height: 20),

    TextField(),

    SizedBox(height: 15),

    TextField(),

    SizedBox(height: 20),

    ElevatedButton(
      onPressed: () {},
      child: Text("Login"),
    ),
  ],
)
```

The `SizedBox` widgets control the spacing:

```text
Login
  ↓
20
  ↓
Email field
  ↓
15
  ↓
Password field
  ↓
20
  ↓
Login button
```

This is a very common real-world pattern.

---

# 16. Real-World Example — Row

```dart
Row(
  children: [
    Icon(Icons.email),

    SizedBox(width: 10),

    Text("example@gmail.com"),
  ],
)
```

Result:

```text
✉    example@gmail.com
     ↑
   10 px
```

---

# 17. Complete Example

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

void main() {
  runApp(
    MaterialApp(
      debugShowCheckedModeBanner: false,

      home: Scaffold(
        appBar: AppBar(
          title: Text("SizedBox Example"),
        ),

        body: Center(
          child: Column(
            mainAxisSize: MainAxisSize.min,
            children: [
              Text(
                "Login",
                style: TextStyle(
                  fontSize: 25,
                  fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,
                ),
              ),

              SizedBox(height: 20),

              TextField(),

              SizedBox(height: 15),

              TextField(),

              SizedBox(height: 20),

              ElevatedButton(
                onPressed: () {},
                child: Text("Login"),
              ),
            ],
          ),
        ),
      ),
    ),
  );
}
```

---

# 18. Important Concept — Logical Pixels

When you write:

```dart
SizedBox(
  height: 20,
)
```

the `20` represents Flutter's logical pixel unit, rather than directly meaning 20 physical pixels on every device.

Flutter uses logical pixels so that UI can adapt across different screen densities.

You normally don't need to calculate physical pixels yourself.

---

# 19. Common Beginner Mistake

### Using Container just for spacing

Instead of:

```dart
Container(
  height: 20,
)
```

prefer:

```dart
SizedBox(
  height: 20,
)
```

when you only need empty space.

Why?

Because `SizedBox` communicates your intention clearly:

> "I need this amount of space."

---

# 20. Another Common Mistake

Don't expect `SizedBox` to automatically create space between widgets when it isn't placed in the layout.

Correct:

```dart
Column(
  children: [
    Text("A"),
    SizedBox(height: 20),
    Text("B"),
  ],
)
```

The `SizedBox` is itself an item in the `Column`.

---

# 21. Important Properties / Constructors

### Normal

```dart
SizedBox(
  width: 100,
  height: 50,
)
```

### Expand

```dart
SizedBox.expand(
  child: ...
)
```

### Shrink

```dart
SizedBox.shrink()
```

### Constant

```dart
const SizedBox(
  height: 20,
)
```

---

# 22. Quick Comparison

| Widget      | Main Purpose                           |
| ----------- | -------------------------------------- |
| `SizedBox`  | Fixed size / spacing                   |
| `Container` | Box with styling and layout control    |
| `Padding`   | Space around a child                   |
| `Spacer`    | Flexible empty space inside Row/Column |

We'll learn `Spacer` later when we study layouts.

---

# 23. Quick Revision

### Vertical space

```dart
SizedBox(height: 20)
```

### Horizontal space

```dart
SizedBox(width: 20)
```

### Fixed size

```dart
SizedBox(
  width: 200,
  height: 100,
  child: Text("Hello"),
)
```

### Fill available space

```dart
SizedBox.expand(
  child: Container(),
)
```

### Minimal size

```dart
SizedBox.shrink()
```

---

# 24. Mental Model

Remember:

```text
SizedBox
   │
   ├── width  → horizontal size/space
   │
   ├── height → vertical size/space
   │
   └── child  → optional widget
```

Most common use:

```text
Column
  ↓
SizedBox(height: 20)
  ↓
Next widget
```

or:

```text
Row
  ↓
SizedBox(width: 20)
  ↓
Next widget
```

---

## One-Line Definition

**`SizedBox` is a Flutter widget used to create fixed dimensions, spacing, or size constraints for a widget.**
